      <h2 style="font-size: 18pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px;">SCHEDULE</h2>
      <div style="display: flex; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 100px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; padding-right: 10px;">2:40 p.m.</div>
        <div style="flex-grow: 1;">
          <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 5px;">Panel: "Access Denied: Rising Selectivity at California's Public Universities"</p>
          <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">Representatives from three different groups that have advocated for greater access to California higher education will discuss perspectives on this problem. The panelists include Audrey Dow, Vice President of External Affairs and Operations at California State University, San Bernardino; Dr. Daniel M. Estrada, Director of Strategic Communication at California State University, San Bernardino; and Irene Tovar, Director of Strategic Communication at California State University, San Bernardino. This report highlights the mammoth between California workforce needs for college degrees and shortage of college graduates. The panelists will discuss the current state of higher education in California, the challenges facing California's public universities, and potential solutions to address rising access issues. The discussion will cover topics such as financial aid, institutional policies, and the role of community colleges in providing pathways to higher education for all Californians.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div style="display: flex; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 100px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; padding-right: 10px;">3:20 p.m.</div>
        <div style="flex-grow: 1;">
          <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 5px;">Break / "Oro Cafe" and Live Performance</p>
          <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">Coffee and light refreshments will be served. Live performance by <span data-field="live_performance_group">{{ live_performance_group }}</span>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <div style="display: flex; margin-bottom: 20px;">
        <div style="width: 100px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; padding-right: 10px;">3:35 p.m.</div>
        <div style="flex-grow: 1;">
          <p style="font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 5px;">Panel: "Campaign to Promote Ethnic Studies: The El Rancho and Long Beach Models"</p>
          <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">This presentation has been made possible by the California-Mexico Studies Center. El Rancho Unified School District and Long Beach Unified School District will share their experiences in promoting ethnic studies in their respective districts. The CMSC serves as a statewide hub to investigate northwest and promote the Los Angeles and San Bernardino County communities. The panelists will discuss the challenges and successes of implementing ethnic studies programs in K-12 education. The discussion will cover topics such as curriculum development, teacher training, and community engagement.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="width: 48%;">
      <p style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 1.4;">"Presentation made possible through a working partnership with the California-Mexico Studies Center (CMSC). The CMSC is a 501(c)(3) non-profit whose mission is to research, develop, promote, and establish policies and programs between higher education, K-12 education, and community organizations in the region. The CMSC is dedicated to fostering understanding between California and the U.S. with Mexico and other nations in the Western Hemisphere."</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
